<title>CHINA: China '96 gold output estimated at 118 tonnes.</title>
<headline>China '96 gold output estimated at 118 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's gold output was estimated at 118 tonnes in 1996, an increase of 10 tonnes compared with 1995, the China Gold newspaper said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The eastern coastal province of Shandong was China's top gold producer in 1996, with output of more than 45 tonnes, said the newspaper, which is published by the Ministry of Metallurgical Industry.</p>
<p>The newspaper gave no further details.</p>
<p>China's gold production surpassed 100 tonnes for the first time in 1995, ranking it sixth in the world after South Africa, the United States, Australia, Russia and Canada.</p>
</text>
